{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Accept the Ass: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja15'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 15 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Sīlavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Ethics </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>5. Kharādiyajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Accept the Ass: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Aṭṭhakkhuraṁ kharādiye, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“Please accept the eight-hooved ass, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>migaṁ vaṅkātivaṅkinaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the deer more wily than the wily.” </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sattahi kālātikkantaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“He has skipped the appointment seven times—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>na naṁ ovaditussahe”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’ll make no attempt to instruct him.” </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Kharādiyajātakaṁ pañcamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
